WEBVTT

00:01.910 --> 00:11.790
While watching anime, make sure not to sit too close to the screen and that the room is well lit.

00:10.270 --> 00:11.600
Begin irradiation.

00:12.100 --> 00:12.320
Roger.

00:24.290 --> 00:28.860
Oh... Your power truly is terrifying, Z2.

00:29.250 --> 00:31.110
I didn't expect this to produce such great results.

00:48.130 --> 00:50.000
Squishy, you're not feeling well...

00:52.890 --> 00:56.430
You're squishy, squishy, and so soft

00:56.810 --> 01:00.330
You're squishy, squishy, and so green

01:00.680 --> 01:04.060
You're squishy, squishy, and the inside of my pochette

01:04.360 --> 01:07.680
Is your favorite place, Squishy!

01:08.890 --> 01:10.100
What's the matter, Eureka?

01:10.560 --> 01:11.590
It's nothing.

01:15.940 --> 01:17.680
Oh! Hey, look! Look!

01:18.000 --> 01:20.250
They're having an exhibit of jewels from all over the world at a hotel!

01:20.490 --> 01:22.340
Oh, I wanna see them!

01:22.600 --> 01:23.340
Jewels?

01:24.600 --> 01:26.090
Let's go have a look!

01:26.090 --> 01:27.180
What do you think?

01:27.180 --> 01:28.540
Please!

01:29.780 --> 01:31.200
Let's go check it out for a bit, then.

01:31.850 --> 01:33.190
All right!

01:33.450 --> 01:34.260
I'm excited!

01:37.600 --> 01:45.050
As Satoshi and his friends continue heading towards the Eisetsu Gym in order to obtain the eighth badge, they make a stop in Jackal Town.

01:54.250 --> 01:59.960
Left and Right!
The Indecisive Kametete!!

02:01.060 --> 02:02.960
It's already over for today?

02:03.510 --> 02:06.420
I'm terribly sorry. Please come again another time.

02:04.920 --> 02:14.850
Play a board game via the Pocket Monsters XY& data broadcast!
Press the d-button on your remote and try reaching the battles and the presents!!

02:04.920 --> 02:14.850
Z

02:06.700 --> 02:08.960
And I was looking forward to it so much...

02:08.960 --> 02:10.720
I got it. Do you have a vacant room?

02:10.990 --> 02:12.430
Yes. We can get one ready for you.

02:13.270 --> 02:16.390
Let's stay here tonight and go see it first thing in the morning.

02:17.500 --> 02:18.440
All right!

02:27.780 --> 02:29.660
I've only got one target...

02:37.480 --> 02:39.860
Let's go to sleep early tonight so we'll be all set and ready tomorrow.

02:40.230 --> 02:40.700
Yeah.

02:43.340 --> 02:43.800
What's this?

02:44.240 --> 02:45.640
It's so loud!

02:45.640 --> 02:47.040
It seems to be an alarm.

02:47.430 --> 02:48.340
On the top floor?

02:48.340 --> 02:49.430
That's where the jewel exhibit is!

02:49.990 --> 02:51.280
"Jewel exhibit", they said.

02:51.600 --> 02:52.660
What on earth...?

02:53.120 --> 02:54.440
We should go have a look, too.

02:54.440 --> 02:54.930
Yeah.

02:57.050 --> 02:58.640
The diamond seems to be safe.

02:59.350 --> 03:01.360
Nothing has been stolen.

03:02.070 --> 03:04.640
This is strange. Why would someone do nothing more than just leave the lock open...?

03:09.530 --> 03:10.280
Who is it?!

03:10.810 --> 03:12.450
I'm the Mysterious Knuckle!

03:12.900 --> 03:16.110
I'm the one who opened the lock to that jewel!

03:22.590 --> 03:23.920
Now then, have a nice day!

03:24.590 --> 03:25.230
Wait!

03:25.500 --> 03:26.760
Call Junsa-san!

03:27.740 --> 03:28.990
"Mysterious Knuckle"...?

03:30.670 --> 03:32.510
This is the Mysterious Knuckle's exact modus operandi.

03:33.790 --> 03:35.300
You saw him too, right?

03:35.900 --> 03:37.860
Can you tell me about what happened?

03:38.090 --> 03:41.400
Yeah! He jumped out of that window and left, like whoosh!

03:41.690 --> 03:45.230
He called himself "Mysterious Knuckle"!

03:47.240 --> 03:48.560
I'm sorry for being late.

03:49.750 --> 03:51.180
Is this the site of the crime?

03:52.340 --> 03:52.720
Yes.

03:53.440 --> 03:54.900
I'm sorry I asked you to come all the way here.

03:55.480 --> 03:55.980
Don't be.

03:56.640 --> 03:57.100
Look at this.

03:59.220 --> 04:02.540
There is no doubt... This is a lock I've made.

04:02.910 --> 04:05.680
Amazing! You made that, gramps?

04:06.730 --> 04:08.040
This is Edo-san, a locksmith.

04:09.580 --> 04:10.560
I'm Satoshi.

04:10.820 --> 04:12.160
This is my partner Pikachu.

04:12.970 --> 04:13.800
I'm Serena.

04:14.040 --> 04:15.100
I'm Eureka.

04:15.420 --> 04:16.840
And this little one is Dedenne.

04:17.720 --> 04:18.630
This is Squishy.

04:18.890 --> 04:19.630
I am Citron.

04:19.980 --> 04:22.340
It's not amazing at all, young lady.

04:22.340 --> 04:22.770
Huh?

04:23.350 --> 04:25.510
It is a fact that it has been picked, see.

04:25.910 --> 04:30.780
The recent crimes committed by the Mysterious Knuckle have all targeted Edo-san's locks.

04:31.420 --> 04:32.750
Huh? Really?

04:33.060 --> 04:34.280
But why...?

04:35.000 --> 04:37.830
The crimes might have been committed out of hate for you, Edo-san.

04:48.870 --> 04:50.130
That's some juicy info.

04:50.500 --> 04:52.810
Let's make the Mysterious Knuckle join us.

04:53.260 --> 04:57.130
With him, we can easily pick even the most complex locks.

04:57.660 --> 04:59.560
This way, we could sneak in everywhere.

04:59.840 --> 05:00.110
Yeah.

05:02.760 --> 05:04.260
That was a surprise!

05:04.260 --> 05:06.650
I never expected us to come across an incident like that.

05:07.150 --> 05:09.680
Now the jewel exhibit has been put on hold for a while...

05:10.270 --> 05:12.190
Geez, blast that Mysterious Knuckle!

05:12.190 --> 05:15.290
I wonder who the Mysterious Knuckle is...

05:22.440 --> 05:23.500
What is this?!

05:23.950 --> 05:26.880
Take it off! Take it off! Take it off!

05:25.470 --> 05:26.320
Eureka!

05:26.320 --> 05:27.320
Wait!

05:29.700 --> 05:30.640
It won't come off!

05:30.640 --> 05:31.840
I will help as well!

05:42.440 --> 05:44.080
Ouch!

05:44.220 --> 05:45.270
Again?!

05:45.500 --> 05:47.620
I'm sick of this!

05:49.480 --> 05:50.940
Ow...

05:50.940 --> 05:53.050
It seems to be complaining about something...

05:53.050 --> 05:53.990
Yeah...

05:54.800 --> 05:56.500
Kametete, the Two-Handed Pokémon.

05:56.940 --> 06:02.890
Two Kametete live together on one rock. When they fight, one of them will move to a different rock.

06:04.980 --> 06:07.670
According to the Zukan, it seems there should be one more.

06:07.670 --> 06:10.340
That is what Kametete should be like, yes.

06:10.340 --> 06:11.180
What's the meaning of this?

06:11.380 --> 06:15.720
It might have something to do with it clinging on to Eureka.

06:16.500 --> 06:17.640
You think so?

06:17.990 --> 06:19.040
Is that you, Right?

06:24.240 --> 06:24.500
Huh?

06:24.960 --> 06:26.620
Is this your Pokémon, Edo-san?

06:26.900 --> 06:27.490
Yeah.

06:28.040 --> 06:29.770
We've had a bit of a fight, you see...

06:30.120 --> 06:31.690
It left after that, and has been gone ever since.

06:32.350 --> 06:33.670
Where have you been?!

06:35.080 --> 06:37.140
I told you to leave him be.

06:37.460 --> 06:39.960
All right, get away from the young lady! We're going home.

06:42.060 --> 06:43.560
You stubborn little...!

06:43.820 --> 06:45.040
Just who do you take after?!

06:46.120 --> 06:48.100
Please, Edo-san, calm down.

06:48.100 --> 06:49.120
She is right!

06:49.340 --> 06:51.680
If you don't mind, could you please tell us why?

06:51.880 --> 06:53.220
It might help us figure something out.

06:55.080 --> 06:56.050
Right over here...

06:57.050 --> 06:59.940
...is looking for a apprentice of mine called Kobushi.

07:06.240 --> 07:07.160
Not like that...

07:08.600 --> 07:09.000
Hey!

07:09.450 --> 07:12.170
If you handle it that roughly, the lock is gonna cry.

07:12.410 --> 07:13.540
But Master...

07:14.150 --> 07:14.910
Give me that.

07:16.180 --> 07:17.640
Don't make me repeat myself.

07:18.340 --> 07:19.860
Locks are like people.

07:20.330 --> 07:22.040
To open a locked heart,

07:22.500 --> 07:24.200
you speak gently with them, right?

07:26.580 --> 07:28.230
You're still lacking training.

07:32.150 --> 07:35.000
Kobushi left not long after that.

07:36.270 --> 07:38.380
He took Left, the other Kametete, with him.

07:38.730 --> 07:39.220
And after that?

07:39.640 --> 07:43.170
Right here insisted it'd look for Left and Kobushi and refused to listen.

07:43.600 --> 07:45.180
I told it to do as it pleases.

07:45.670 --> 07:49.690
I don't have enough free time I can look after someone who left of their own accord.

07:50.410 --> 07:53.060
So that's why Right is still angry.

07:53.340 --> 07:54.510
I see...

07:55.530 --> 07:58.360
Right! Stop causing her trouble!

07:58.750 --> 08:00.090
Get away from the young lady!

08:02.150 --> 08:02.760
You little...!

08:03.120 --> 08:04.950
Wait! Please calm down!

08:05.480 --> 08:08.970
Could we please borrow Right, just for today?

08:08.970 --> 08:09.710
Yeah, can we?

08:10.150 --> 08:11.670
Hm? Borrow?

08:12.260 --> 08:14.040
I'll take care of it!

08:17.300 --> 08:19.220
Only for one day, Right.

08:19.710 --> 08:21.380
Don't cause them trouble.

08:22.460 --> 08:22.990
All right!

08:23.290 --> 08:26.330
Now that that's decided, let's go look for Kobushi-san and Left tomorrow!

08:26.680 --> 08:27.680
Yeah!

08:36.950 --> 08:39.150
You really are a troublesome apprentice.

08:40.250 --> 08:42.110
I haven't told anyone besides you...

08:43.350 --> 08:45.800
...how to undo this lock,

08:46.360 --> 08:47.290
Kobushi.

08:50.810 --> 08:55.780
If Master Edo sees that lock, he'll have no choice but to acknowledge my prowess.

08:58.100 --> 08:59.400
I know, Left.

08:59.770 --> 09:01.780
It's only when I'm with you that I'm a full-fledged locksmith.

09:05.550 --> 09:07.620
I've found the other Kametete!

09:08.060 --> 09:10.730
That guy who's with it must be the Mysterious Knuckle.

09:10.730 --> 09:12.100
All right, capture him!

09:12.750 --> 09:13.480
Roger!

09:19.060 --> 09:19.830
What's this?!

09:21.440 --> 09:23.130
So you're the Mysterious Knuckle.

09:23.420 --> 09:24.360
What do you guys want?

09:25.190 --> 09:26.900
If it's jewels, I have none!

09:27.350 --> 09:28.870
I don't steal!

09:29.290 --> 09:31.130
We don't care about that.

09:31.130 --> 09:32.790
Our plans involve <i>you</i>...

09:33.100 --> 09:34.580
...and your partner Kametete.

09:34.870 --> 09:35.460
What?!

09:41.620 --> 09:44.590
All right, let's go find Kobushi-san and Left!

09:45.540 --> 09:47.710
...That said, I have no idea where to look.

09:47.940 --> 09:49.920
We need clues of some sort...

09:49.920 --> 09:52.270
Heh, it seems like my turn has come.

09:52.920 --> 09:55.220
It is time for science to open up the future!

09:55.520 --> 09:57.520
Citronic Gear on!

09:57.900 --> 10:00.820
For moments like this, I have prepared a nice machine.

10:00.820 --> 10:02.340
This is the Kametete Detector!

10:02.820 --> 10:05.050
Another name that's just a description...

10:06.250 --> 10:08.790
It is actually not made specifically for Kametete,

10:09.040 --> 10:10.730
but given the occasion, we might as well call it that.

10:10.730 --> 10:11.620
That's so halfhearted...

10:12.580 --> 10:13.930
This will help us find them, right?

10:13.930 --> 10:14.410
Yes!

10:14.870 --> 10:21.880
Kametete come in pairs, so it just needs to find a Pokémon with the same biometric data as Right.

10:22.990 --> 10:24.470
Switch on!

10:26.280 --> 10:27.680
Now it should be okay.

10:27.680 --> 10:30.740
Wow! Technology really is incredible!

10:32.660 --> 10:34.680
I got it! This way!

10:35.240 --> 10:36.600
We'll find them in no time, Right!

10:42.520 --> 10:43.910
Pokémon Quiz.

10:44.160 --> 10:45.020
The answer is...?

10:55.990 --> 10:56.630
This is...

10:57.130 --> 10:58.870
The back of the Pokémon Center, yeah.

10:59.370 --> 11:03.620
We want to open this storage and take all the Pokémon inside.

11:04.630 --> 11:06.510
Yep, that's exactly it.

11:06.960 --> 11:08.640
It should be a piece of cake for you, shouldn't it?

11:09.950 --> 11:12.090
Got it. I'll do it.

11:12.460 --> 11:13.610
All right!

11:15.720 --> 11:17.720
Hey, remove this rope.

11:18.110 --> 11:19.270
I can't use my hands otherwise.

11:19.770 --> 11:21.190
I guess we have no choice.

11:21.190 --> 11:22.750
Nyarth, take it off.

11:22.750 --> 11:23.770
Sure!

11:26.090 --> 11:27.360
Left, let's do this.

11:31.340 --> 11:33.450
Now we'll get a big load of Pokémon!

11:33.980 --> 11:35.410
Or so you thought...

11:35.720 --> 11:37.480
I don't steal!

11:37.480 --> 11:38.280
Brick Break!

11:42.460 --> 11:43.830
Hey, Nyarth!

11:43.830 --> 11:44.590
Let's go, Left!

11:46.100 --> 11:47.420
We won't let you get away!

11:47.990 --> 11:49.870
Go, Pumpjin!

11:51.860 --> 11:53.050
Maaiika, you too!

11:55.850 --> 11:56.720
Seed Bomb!

11:56.720 --> 11:58.020
Psybeam!

12:00.500 --> 12:01.100
Whoa!

12:05.290 --> 12:06.440
Hey, you are...

12:07.030 --> 12:09.060
Joy-san, please call Junsa-san!

12:09.440 --> 12:11.150
Those guys are trying to steal the Pokémon here...

12:12.460 --> 12:13.540
Psybeam!

12:12.460 --> 12:13.280
Seed Bomb!

12:27.550 --> 12:29.610
This feels bad!

12:44.640 --> 12:45.160
Is that...

12:45.630 --> 12:46.310
...fire?!

12:47.370 --> 12:49.120
The device is pointing towards that place!

12:49.370 --> 12:50.000
No way!

12:50.000 --> 12:50.860
Let's hurry!

12:51.800 --> 12:52.380
This is terrible!

12:52.830 --> 12:53.610
Watch out!

12:53.900 --> 12:57.080
But... There are many Pokémon in there!

13:00.720 --> 13:01.440
This is bad.

13:03.080 --> 13:03.880
Joy-san!

13:09.110 --> 13:09.620
Right?

13:10.090 --> 13:10.980
You're Kobushi-san, right?

13:11.360 --> 13:12.170
Y-Yeah...

13:12.560 --> 13:15.470
Right has been looking for you and Left the whole time.

13:15.930 --> 13:16.580
For us?

13:17.690 --> 13:19.320
Kobushi-san, we'll tell you about it later.

13:19.740 --> 13:21.850
Right now we need to focus on putting out the fire!

13:21.850 --> 13:22.310
Yeah.

13:23.580 --> 13:25.630
Joy-san, do you have the key for that door?

13:25.980 --> 13:28.600
The explosion just now made me drop and lose sight of it.

13:29.000 --> 13:31.400
Then please call the fire department.

13:31.400 --> 13:31.780
Yeah!

13:32.960 --> 13:33.590
Kobushi-san...

13:33.940 --> 13:35.260
There are Pokémon in there.

13:36.640 --> 13:38.050
Me and my partner can do this!

13:39.150 --> 13:40.480
We'll rescue everyone, just watch.

13:41.590 --> 13:42.790
Let's go, partner!

13:43.500 --> 13:44.110
Kobushi-san!

13:47.910 --> 13:48.630
Watch out!

13:48.920 --> 13:50.770
Everyone, let's stop the momentum of the fire!

13:51.220 --> 13:52.600
Gekkouga, Water Shuriken!

13:57.930 --> 13:58.710
Here!

13:58.710 --> 13:59.580
Hang in there!

14:02.030 --> 14:03.720
Right, can you do a Water Gun?

14:05.100 --> 14:05.850
Please!

14:11.310 --> 14:12.680
Kobushi-san, now's your chance!

14:16.600 --> 14:19.540
All right. Let's do this, Left. Same procedure as every time.

14:25.920 --> 14:26.800
Everyone, hang in there!

14:28.190 --> 14:30.160
Right, keep using Water Gun!

14:44.740 --> 14:45.400
We did it.

14:49.290 --> 14:50.090
All right, Left.

14:50.420 --> 14:52.160
Fill this with the monster balls!

15:09.110 --> 15:09.900
It won't open!

15:10.630 --> 15:12.130
Hey, can you hear me?! Hey!

15:12.700 --> 15:13.220
Yes!

15:13.510 --> 15:14.910
The door won't open!

15:15.130 --> 15:15.930
What did you say?!

15:18.980 --> 15:20.360
What now, bro...?

15:20.900 --> 15:22.160
What now, Eureka...?

15:24.240 --> 15:25.990
Eureka, where are you going?

15:25.990 --> 15:27.430
Ask Right!

15:32.490 --> 15:33.940
There are Pokémon in there.

15:33.940 --> 15:34.650
Understood.

15:38.040 --> 15:38.860
What?

15:40.060 --> 15:40.860
Whoa!

15:40.860 --> 15:42.520
The young lady and Right?

15:46.340 --> 15:47.450
What happened?

15:58.580 --> 15:59.770
Is everyone all right?

16:01.210 --> 16:02.430
Eureka! Edo-san!

16:02.820 --> 16:05.980
I see. So Right went to get Edo-san.

16:05.980 --> 16:07.930
Edo-san, the key for the storage door...

16:08.140 --> 16:09.440
Yeah, I heard the whole story.

16:10.110 --> 16:11.560
All right. Time for work, Right!

16:12.660 --> 16:13.280
Edo-san!

16:14.100 --> 16:15.850
It's dangerous! Don't get any closer!

16:15.850 --> 16:18.100
Don't interfere! My apprentice is in trouble!

16:18.660 --> 16:20.490
Uh... Hey, sir!

16:25.190 --> 16:26.500
Kobushi! Kobushi!

16:26.720 --> 16:28.060
Can you hear me? It's me!

16:28.300 --> 16:28.880
Master?

16:29.760 --> 16:33.050
Don't tell me, you, a locksmith, have given up on trying to open something!

16:33.590 --> 16:35.240
We can open anything.

16:35.520 --> 16:36.960
I've taught you that, haven't I?

16:37.750 --> 16:38.430
Master...

16:38.980 --> 16:39.980
Can you move your hands?

16:42.010 --> 16:43.780
I was just taking a short break.

16:44.160 --> 16:45.320
Left, let's do this!

16:46.240 --> 16:47.100
That's rich.

16:47.440 --> 16:51.020
Let's try this simultaneously; me from outside and you from inside.

16:51.020 --> 16:51.450
Yes.

16:51.700 --> 16:53.360
Can you see the rotary discs?

16:53.360 --> 16:53.810
Yes.

16:54.240 --> 16:55.500
This will be a difficult task.

16:56.010 --> 16:57.520
There are five rotary discs inside.

16:58.070 --> 16:59.820
Dial the second hindmost to the right by two,

17:00.320 --> 17:02.510
and the frontmost one to the left by one.

17:02.940 --> 17:05.030
Finally, dial the middle one to the right by one.

17:05.380 --> 17:07.140
I'll keep the deformed parts supported.

17:07.780 --> 17:08.910
Right, lend me a hand.

17:10.300 --> 17:10.790
All right.

17:11.420 --> 17:13.240
Come on, Kobushi! We don't have time!

17:13.530 --> 17:14.040
Okay!

17:14.470 --> 17:15.670
I'm counting on you, Left.

17:20.580 --> 17:23.210
Take a deep breath and calm down.

17:24.680 --> 17:27.120
Handle the lock gently.

17:36.720 --> 17:37.350
Master,

17:37.920 --> 17:41.340
in case I can't get out of here, there's something I want to tell you.

17:41.340 --> 17:43.290
Shut up and move your hands!

17:44.260 --> 17:47.880
I'm the Mysterious Knuckle who went around opening your locks, Master.

17:48.520 --> 17:50.910
I wanted you to approve of me...

17:51.270 --> 17:52.550
I knew.

17:53.580 --> 17:55.260
Do you need me to spell it out for you?

17:55.900 --> 17:58.390
You're the only one besides me who...

17:58.790 --> 18:01.080
...possesses the skill to open those locks.

18:01.940 --> 18:04.710
You are already a fine locksmith.

18:07.120 --> 18:07.910
Master...

18:18.430 --> 18:21.160
Kobushi, listen! This is the hard part!

18:21.480 --> 18:22.440
Yes, Master!

18:37.230 --> 18:39.180
That was nice work, my apprentice.

18:40.030 --> 18:41.150
Yes, Master!

18:49.520 --> 18:51.780
I can't believe Kobushi-san was the Mysterious Knuckle...

18:52.200 --> 18:53.980
Did you know, Edo-san?

18:54.190 --> 18:54.810
Yeah.

18:55.460 --> 18:58.230
I'm really sorry to have caused you so much trouble.

18:58.830 --> 19:01.520
You alone must atone for your own crimes.

19:01.960 --> 19:02.230
Yes.

19:07.040 --> 19:08.600
Thank you, Left.

19:10.550 --> 19:13.000
Let's go. I'll ask about the details at the station.

19:13.720 --> 19:15.750
When you're a free man, come back.

19:16.350 --> 19:19.140
I'll always be waiting for you with unlocked doors.

19:21.340 --> 19:22.060
Master...

19:28.990 --> 19:30.510
I'm so glad for Kobushi-san.

19:30.790 --> 19:33.150
Me too. He has a place to come back to.

19:33.380 --> 19:36.400
Surely, he will become a good locksmith. He has the talent, after all.

19:36.990 --> 19:39.840
You see, this is just between us, but the truth is...

19:41.080 --> 19:46.320
All the Mysterious Knuckle did was open locks, so he'll only get a stern warning and then immediately get sent home.

19:47.120 --> 19:48.550
I'm sorry for the inconvenience.

19:50.310 --> 19:51.080
Really?

19:51.520 --> 19:55.700
I thought he'd learn his lesson better if I didn't tell him about it.

19:58.960 --> 20:04.110
Having witnessed the bond between master and apprentice and between humans and Pokémon,

20:04.550 --> 20:08.060
Satoshi and his friends once again realized the importance of relationships based on mutual trust.

20:09.110 --> 20:10.420
Satoshi and his friends' journey is...

20:15.920 --> 20:20.920
Pokémon no Uchi Atsumaru?

20:15.920 --> 20:20.920
Sunday March 13th at 8am

20:15.920 --> 20:19.090
Foodin

20:16.490 --> 20:19.090
Using magic to replicate "Confusion"!

20:16.920 --> 20:19.090
Pokémon magic at Pokénchi!

20:19.090 --> 20:20.920
What?

20:19.460 --> 20:20.920
Whaat!?

20:23.550 --> 20:25.940
Pokémon Unbelievable!

20:26.860 --> 20:32.240
This is Pokémon Unbelievable, which features the mysterious ecology of Pokémon!

20:33.070 --> 20:40.550
1 Kametete

20:33.070 --> 20:40.550
"2" becomes "1"!? The Mystery of Kametete!!

20:33.500 --> 20:37.880
Two Kametete attached to one rock are...

20:38.270 --> 20:40.470
...seen as one Pokémon.

20:41.800 --> 20:48.130
Its evolved form Gamenodes, on the other hand, is formed by seven Kametete who fulfill the functions of hands and feet,

20:48.710 --> 20:50.140
again acting as one single Pokémon.

20:51.180 --> 20:55.800
However, there is a theory that the Kametete might fight among each other and come apart again.

20:57.570 --> 21:02.390
By the way, this Gamenodes is said to be extremely strong at rock-paper-scissors.

21:02.710 --> 21:04.090
Let's try this right away.

21:04.920 --> 21:07.500
